            "review_text": "davidtran95\nManila, Philippines87 contributions\n0\nPao down\nDec 2012 • Solo\nFor the life of me, I don’t know why this restaurant received so many high marks. I ordered Vietnamese fried spring rolls, but they came out burned. I also ordered seafood fried noodles, but I found it a little too greasy and they weren’t very generous with the seafood either, which didn’t even taste fresh (listen chef: you are using old cooking oil). On the other hand, I noticed that the waiters there were very attentive and quick. The restaurant is open, facing the street, so you can sit down and have a beer while watching the city life pass by but other than that, I wouldn’t recommend to eat at this place.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten April 30, 2013",
