            "review_text": "Tim B\nDorchester, United Kingdom38 contributions\n0\nWell-placed and OK for the price\nDec 2012 • Friends\nWe have eaten three times in this restaurant, which is in the heart of the backpackers area (Bui Vien). Pao Cafe has some comfortable chairs (and tables) facing the street - definitely the best place to be seated. \n\nThere doesn't seem to be any really good restaurant in the Pham Ngu Lao area, although it's a fun place to eat or have a drink, as it's buzzing with activity. Pao cafe itself has perfectly OK food at good prices, perhaps slightly better than the average in the area. Dishes like beef or chicken with lemon grass and chillies, or crab fried rice or various noodle dishes are all fresh and good, though not outstanding. If you opt for a fresh lime soda, then make sure to ask for extra limes and sugar when you've finished your glass, with over half of the soda can remaining. Then it's excellent value. \n\nPao Cafe is a nice place to see life go by on Bui Vien Street. Recommended.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 10, 2012",
            "rating": 5.0,
