            "review_title": "Review at Pao Cafe",
            "review_text": "LimaJuliet_AUS\n11 contributions\n0\nNo better than an average suburban Chinese takeaway\nWe visited Pao Cafe for lunch today as it was the best reviwed Vietnamese eatery near our hotel. Granted, we are staying in the backpacker district and there are squillions of Italian and Mexican places and English pubs. When we arrived at Pao Cafe, it was deserted, aside from the staff, so I ordered spring rolls and a prawn and broccoli dish.The food took absolutely forever to come out and, when it finally arrived, was very disappointing. The spring rolls were served with a mayonnaise dipping sauce (hardly authentic Vietnamese) and the prawns were no better than what I can get from any old suburban Chinese place back in Australia!!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 25, 2012",
